@startuml
autonumber
box "Kubernetes Master" #LightBlue
participant "Kubernetes API" as K8S_API
end box

box "Kubernetes namespace (PODs)" #LightYellow
  participant InitContainer
  participant Application
  participant Postgres
end box

box "Vault Components" #LightGreen
  participant "Vault Key-Value" as VaultSecretStore
  participant "Vault Transit" as TransitSigningEngine
  participant "Vault PKI" as VaultPKI
  actor "Secrets Manager" as SSM
end box

group Application PODs bootstrap & Secrets Initialization

K8S_API -> InitContainer: Start Pod \nservice account JWT
InitContainer -> VaultSecretStore: Fetch secrets using Kubernetes Authentication
note over VaultSecretStore #pink
<b>Sensitive config:</b>
kubernetes_host (https)
end note 
VaultSecretStore -> K8S_API: Verify JWT token
note over K8S_API
  For more information:
  [[https://developer.hashicorp.com/vault/docs/auth/kubernetes#how-to-work-with-short-lived-kubernetes-tokens Kubernetes short lived tokens for Vault]].
end note
K8S_API -> VaultSecretStore: Token Valid 
VaultSecretStore -> InitContainer: Return secrets
note right of VaultSecretStore #pink
<b>Threat:</b> privilege escalation due to wide access to secrets
<b>Mitigation:</b> minimal secre access to Application
end note
InitContainer -> Application: Store secrets in Pod environment
note right of Application #pink
  <b>Threat:</b> Secret disclosure
  <b>Mitigation:</b> volatile protected environment
end note
' deactivate VaultSecretStore
' destroy VaultSecretStore
note right of K8S_API #pink
<b>Threat:</b> Token theft
<b>Mitigation:</b> short lived tokens
end note
K8S_API -> K8S_API: JWT token expires
destroy InitContainer

group Extra initialization and health check (not in place, necessary for secure key rotation)
Application -> VaultSecretStore: Fetch Postgres creds
Application -> Posrgres: Test Postgres connection
Application -> VaultSecretStore: Fetch Root of trust(s) for PKI
Application -> VaultSecretStore: Fetch Transit keys
Application -> TransitSigningEngine: Test successful signature service (on a well and sale hardcoded or empty message)
Application -> Application: Test signature verification with Root of trust for PKI
activate Application
Application -> VaultPKI: Fetch intermediate CA certificates
Application -> Application: Use inertmediate CA certificates to verify previously signed dummy message
Application -> Application: Set Health check to OK
deactivate Application
end group 

end group
== Signing operations using Vault Transit Secret Engine ==

Application -> TransitSigningEngine: Login with username and password
TransitSigningEngine -> Application: Return access token

Application -> TransitSigningEngine: Perform signing operations with access token

alt On token expiry
    Application -> TransitSigningEngine: Login with username and password
    TransitSigningEngine -> Application: Return new access token
end
== Example Postgres Credential Use ==

Application -> Postgres: DB Connect using credentials from Vault

== Verification operations using Vault PKI Secret Engine ==

Application -> VaultPKI: Login with username and password
VaultPKI -> Application: Return access token

Application -> VaultPKI: Get public certificates or check signature (with access token)

alt On token expiry
    Application -> VaultPKI: Login with username and password
    VaultPKI -> Application: Return new access token
end



== Secret Rotation Process (Postgres example) ==
group For: On failure during restart (not in place)
  SSM -> VaultSecretStore: Fetch old Postgres credentials 
  VaultSecretStore -> SSM: Return old Postgres credentials and store in volatile memory 
end

SSM -> Postgres: Create Additional valid new Posrgres credentials
activate SSM
SSM -> VaultSecretStore: Set new Postgres credentials in Vault

SSM -> VaultSecretStore: Create new VaultSecretStore username/password pair
note over VaultSecretStore
  Any newly started Application (POD) will
   pick up this new Postgres credentials. 
   Old client will fail to retrieve credentials 
   (if trying, they should not by design: only at init)
end note
' VaultSecretStore -> SSM: Return new credentials
' SSM -> VaultSecretStore: Update secrets in Vault
VaultSecretStore -> SSM: Confirm update

SSM -> K8S_API: Gradually Restart Pods to pick up new credentials
====== REPEAT: Application PODs bootstrap & Secrets Initialization [...] ==
alt Successfullt health from Pods
group health check (not in place)
SSM -> Application: Health check?
Application -> SSM: Health check OK
end 

K8S_API -> SSM: Confirm all Pods restarted and have new credentials
note left of  SSM #pink
  <b>Threat:</b> DoS on POD startup failure
   after cred rotation (e.g. Postgres)
  <b>Mitigation:</b> gradual restarts
  <b>Mitigation:</b> at least 2 PODs per service
  <b>Mitigation:</b> health checks (not in place)
  <b>Mitigation:</b> rollback on failure (not in place)
end note

else On failure during restart (not in place)
  SSM -> VaultSecretStore: Fetch old Postgres credentials
  VaultSecretStore -> SSM: Return old Postgres credentials
  SSM -> Postgres: Reset old Postgres credentials
  Postgres -> SSM: Confirm reset
  SSM -> K8S_API: Rollback Pods to use old credentials
end
SSM -> Postgres: Revoke old Postgres credentials
' Postgres -> SSM: Confirm revocation
deactivate SSM
== Example Postgres Credential Use ==

Application -> Postgres: DB Connect using rotated credentials from Vault


@enduml
